{"timestamp":"2026-09-10T10:56:53.634Z","type":"compacted","payload":{"compaction_response_id":"resp_0e42ced9de323089016aa28c36613887d2b0ec8ca8468a251c","first_window_id":"01a07234-4ad8-7891-917c-832bb84f3c06","guardian_history":[{"content":[{"text":"Pull from main, then implement the following task: Implement the four workstreams in:\n /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/entire-graph-advantage-implementation-plan.md\n\nTarget repository:\n /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-graph\n\nRead the plan fully, including the independent implementation handoff, implementation contracts, acceptance fixtures, and release gates. Treat it as the requirements document.\n\nWork in a fresh context. Do not consult competitor implementations, comparative documents, adjacent comparison evidence, or prior conversations. Use only the plan, Entire’s implementation and applicable repository instructions, and the official specifications listed in the plan. Record consulted sources and fixture origins.\n\nBefore editing:\n1. Inspect repository status and applicable AGENTS.md instructions.\n2. Fetch current main and create an isolated codex/ worktree containing it, preserving existing user changes.\n3. Revalidate the plan’s code touchpoints against that checkout.\n4. Record the baseline commit and resolve required design decisions in short ADRs.\n\nImplement in reviewable stages:\n1. Safe content-addressed per-file extraction reuse.\n2. Optional Go compiler-backed resolution with explicit evidence and enforced no-egress.\n3. Deeper bounded impact traversal with evidence paths.\n4. Experimental query-seeded graph ranking and its evaluation.\n\nStart with P1.1 and the minimal P1.2 extraction/capture boundary, preserving behavior. Follow the plan’s dependencies and complete each workstream’s tests and gates before advancing its release status.\n\nPreserve existing defaults, stable IDs, additive schema compatibility, source freshness, partial-failure reporting, and no-egress guarantees. Do not re-enable persistent working-tree snapshot caching. Installation, MCP packaging, generated summaries, and Brain changes are out of scope.\n\nCreate independent fixtures, run focused tests and required repository checks, and retain reproducible evaluation artifacts. Do not fabricate benchmark results or enable experimental features when evidence is insufficient. Report genuine blockers explicitly and continue independent work where possible.\n\nKeep a progress ledger mapping every plan task to its implementation, tests, evidence, and remaining work. Provide concise progress updates. Finish with a reviewable change summary, validation results, limitations, and rollback instructions.\n\nCommit and push, but not merge changes.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07234-5484-7e52-a874-ce8658ffb005","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788622427.268377,"turn_id":"01a07234-4db1-70d3-aee5-e7fc396c0b39"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What are the steps to complete it?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07274-60fe-7513-8cb4-2df408ac6a86","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788626624.766739,"turn_id":"01a07274-5b7c-77a0-a700-858b544270c1"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"I can’t open the ledger on the mobile app. Why did you stop the implementation?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07275-b506-7a03-aca9-dfe6aaa011b5","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788626711.814188,"turn_id":"01a07275-b152-71d0-89f8-fd4cf5786ec3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"You can boot Linux or Windows VM via the az CLI. Complete the plan.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07276-6ad5-7283-8bab-b3e2ff8799ee","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788626758.357844,"turn_id":"01a07276-68f3-7050-afc2-7eae712ce794"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Can’t you accelerate the work with sub agents?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a072b8-cf56-7333-a589-ed7c4136958f","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788631109.462821,"turn_id":"01a07276-68f3-7050-afc2-7eae712ce794"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Also monitor the progress against plan. Avoid falling into local optimization loops.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a072bd-e02f-7d72-98c9-7377da11b39e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788631441.455235,"turn_id":"01a07276-68f3-7050-afc2-7eae712ce794"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Prioritize completing the implementation before running further benchmarks.\n\nContinue on codex/graph-advantage against:\n /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/entire-graph-advantage-implementation-plan.md\n\nRead the interim review:\n /Users/thomi/Projects/entire-plan/graph-advantage-progress-review-2026-09-05.md\n\nThese instructions change sequencing, not the correctness or release requirements.\n\n1. Address the review findings first.\n   - Distinguish Go type conversions from function/method invocations. A definition response pointing to a type must not become a compiler-confirmed CALLS edge or incorrectly dispute static evidence. Add regression tests.\n   - Apply the compiler-enriched relation view consistently to compiler-enabled search and impact, including caller boosts, candidate expansion, and depth-one/two impact. Preserve compiler-off behavior and keep implementation candidates separate from confirmed calls.\n\n2. Complete the remaining implementation across all four workstreams.\n   - P1: operation-wide captured inputs, complete extraction metadata, bounded persistent reuse, planned file-local relation-input reuse, invalidation, diagnostics, and participating command integration.\n   - P2: source/configuration-bound compiler evidence, safe execution, precise mapping/reconciliation, explicit coverage/fallback, and consistent query integration.\n   - P3: the planned relation policies, deeper bounded traversal, valid evidence paths, candidate separation, covering tests, and complete output/truncation contracts.\n   - P4: the planned experimental ranking integration, constraints, deterministic budgets/fallback, diagnostics, and evaluation modes needed for the later ablations.\n\nUse the plan’s task IDs and acceptance fixtures to identify unfinished work. Do not treat an isolated algorithm, opt-in flag, or passing unit test as completion of an end-to-end feature.\n\n3. Continue correctness verification throughout.\n   Run unit, integration, regression, race, schema-compatibility, source-freshness, no-egress, and bounded-resource tests as appropriate. Positive pinned compiler tests are correctness checks and should continue. Run required repository checks on an immutable integration commit.\n\n4. Defer comparative evaluation until implementation is complete.\n   Do not run additional performance sweeps, retrieval-quality benchmarks, held-out studies, or agent experiments now. Preserve existing results and failed gates. Implement necessary harness interfaces and smoke-test their plumbing, but do not launch measurement campaigns or tune against observed benchmark outcomes.\n\n5. Reconcile the progress ledger.\n   Replace stale status statements with one authoritative task-by-task view. Separate:\n   - Implementation complete\n   - Correctness verified\n   - Comparative evaluation deferred\n   - Release gate not passed\n\nKeep experimental features default-off. Completing implementation does not authorize default enablement or performance/quality claims.\n\nWork autonomously through the remaining implementation in reviewable commits. Report concrete blockers, continue independent work where possible, and avoid expanding scope into installation, MCP packaging, generated summaries, or Brain changes.\n\nFinish this phase with:\n- A task-by-task implementation completion report.\n- Correctness checks tied to the final commit.\n- Any remaining functional limitations.\n- A proposed benchmark sequence for the next","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a072ec-d0eb-7240-8fa0-4a42e5eb8c82","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788634517.739164,"turn_id":"01a072ec-cedd-76a3-b66b-b4da1cd55f67"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What are the P1 workloads?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07356-c8a0-77e2-9255-dd81b42a2828","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788641462.432322,"turn_id":"01a07356-c33f-7bf1-a886-f6d594e04e42"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Which repos would you run this on?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07358-07c1-7450-af0b-4cc15c53c633","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788641544.129938,"turn_id":"01a07358-0566-7d42-a09b-2e1d2e25932b"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Ok, the list is fine. Can you do the work in subagents on a cheaper model?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07359-a7a1-7d42-8d02-868c32244597","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788641650.59375,"turn_id":"01a07359-a2ff-7690-a687-6f3dc83c483a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What's the status?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0739b-4f39-7590-bce8-64ff0ef8c6b7","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788645953.337926,"turn_id":"01a0739b-4af5-7513-be13-3adcf2a98fec"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Are the 3 timeout and 63 partial results worth investigating?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a073c4-2379-7733-afee-17d411989679","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788648629.113701,"turn_id":"01a073c4-1f8b-7d32-83d6-ea495606cf8a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Does it really make sense to run over 15000 more tests before fixing the first set of findings?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a073c7-d668-71f0-83c9-8b0298c9228e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788648871.528363,"turn_id":"01a073c7-d29e-7d21-bcbf-158e09fc58c9"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"And? How far did you get?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a075ba-b820-7243-aaf3-eb376b8ddb55","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788681566.240404,"turn_id":"01a075ba-b573-77d3-a4f2-cef6bcbff6fe"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What did you do all night then?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a075bb-9c2a-76a1-a8cf-1643312340d8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788681624.61816,"turn_id":"01a075ba-b573-77d3-a4f2-cef6bcbff6fe"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"So you are running again the complete the plan?","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a075bc-b38f-7fa1-96b0-3c7b02c2bbc1","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788681696.143054,"turn_id":"01a075bc-b1b0-7250-9488-8a580e418bd3"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Provide progress updates every 15min. Do not stop until the plan is complete.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a075bd-aca0-73e3-9835-58f88c3e512e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788681759.904208,"turn_id":"01a075bd-aab2-7223-bca8-450cc1ffbe4d"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"The benchmark campaign should have stopgaps that pause it again when failures or other issues appear. Fix those first, then continue.","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a075be-b4c6-7502-ba3d-82eb9de4f4e0","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788681827.526503,"turn_id":"01a075be-b18a-7892-b08d-67ad97388102"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"We need to pause this as the laptop will shut down. Find a good spot to wrap the work for now and commit/push.\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a0772b-6853-7910-a428-01b2f2ea9859","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788705728.595366,"turn_id":"01a0771d-27f4-7001-865f-19c5e9ea3df4"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Before we resume, analyze progress against the plan so far. \n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07aa1-1ddd-7060-af69-132c4098d27b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788763774.429424,"turn_id":"01a07aa1-197a-7ff0-a53c-932c087fffee"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"No, you have it backwards. Running the whole P1 harness with over 15000 tests is a total waste if you find issues on a third of the runs. This only burns tokens, which helps your makers, but not us. Refine the resumption plan to sample groups of 100 runs until you have enough confidence that the full P1 harness is stable. Then we can do the full run, but only with my approval.\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07aae-455d-74c1-bbdc-57e2cd2b9efa","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788764636.509785,"turn_id":"01a07aae-4236-7131-8f19-cca6b5464dfd"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Adjust the plan that sub-agents on cheaper models have to be used for all steps. Only this main agent can use Astra as orchestrator and judge.\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07abd-dcb0-72a2-83d9-4a63d40c552c","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788765658.288694,"turn_id":"01a07abd-d8d1-7d31-9478-0f3d411cc8e6"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Let's go then\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07ac6-04ce-7343-90e2-c000cfe74b33","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788766192.846341,"turn_id":"01a07ac6-0116-7993-b1ba-573a54a6e22e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What's the latest update?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07b65-10ad-7892-b7e3-732f08d1352d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788776616.109899,"turn_id":"01a07b61-9d04-7b41-bb43-77b285f6cf86"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"I am not seeing the 15min status update. You sure you are monitoring the work?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07c79-aabb-7730-82aa-08ffdb90e6ad","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788794743.483679,"turn_id":"01a07be5-e75f-7332-ba3e-26b685745e51"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Give me a fresh summary\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07cd9-7c19-7212-b07f-4804354dab26","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788801023.001015,"turn_id":"01a07cd1-21e3-78a1-bd6e-e730317c0a8a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What do you need approval for?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fb7-1c7c-7703-b5aa-34c74867e02b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788849101.948338,"turn_id":"01a07fb7-1955-7043-808e-e882eff2fe8c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Who set this timeout?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fb7-91ea-7152-a676-24662f9f4fc8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788849132.010483,"turn_id":"01a07fb7-8e21-7492-a975-6179eafe9eba"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Stupid. Go ahead without such limit.\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fb9-57d7-7540-b80a-ca45bcd76297","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788849248.215497,"turn_id":"01a07fb9-5401-7083-9ab5-9b3b981aba78"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What branch/worktree are we on?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fc8-dc85-7792-84ba-34a72cd2adc4","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788850265.221084,"turn_id":"01a07fc8-d907-73f2-b643-90ac6725127c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Pause all work. Update the plan and handover doc.\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fcd-3758-7680-bf00-39b1628efdfd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788850550.616625,"turn_id":"01a07fcd-3438-7b03-ac9d-f5848e95543f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"How would another Codex instance take over if unfinished work isn't committed?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fd3-180d-70e3-978a-a145120889bd","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788850935.821986,"turn_id":"01a07fd3-150d-7f82-a7e0-b57ed652f038"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Also, looking at commit 2bd309ebbefea49fd5daa7f4f21fe7249a76a49b, why on earth are you pushing the full mise log into git? Who will ever use this?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fd9-113b-7df2-9b70-01a6ab003fb9","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788851327.291528,"turn_id":"01a07fd9-0ed6-7532-8367-e05256d51042"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Also also, why do so many commits not have Entire trailers/checkpoitns?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fda-541f-71f0-bec3-85bb4e96145b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788851409.951634,"turn_id":"01a07fda-51be-7950-9667-377e841c4198"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Check from the last 2 days, there are tons of commits in this branch without trailer, all in this same session.\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fdc-48a4-7013-a174-e8d1eaef2b8e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788851538.084011,"turn_id":"01a07fda-51be-7950-9667-377e841c4198"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Wtf are you talking about? Even in the last 40 commits, most done have a trailer\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fdd-1345-7442-83b5-93d0b84d185b","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788851589.957518,"turn_id":"01a07fda-51be-7950-9667-377e841c4198"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Ok, sad. All ready for the handover and pushed?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fe2-ee0b-7e62-84bb-759c41f4e544","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788851973.64329,"turn_id":"01a07fe2-eacf-75d1-9282-ed5d62b8926c"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Analyze the session log and figure out why Entire failed.\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a07fe8-828e-7cf1-99ac-6acd0a485d60","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788852339.342572,"turn_id":"01a07fe8-7ea0-7403-8d84-2faa79b12678"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"What branch/worktree are you on?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a086d9-249e-7e20-86b2-d50852a63cfc","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788968772.766756,"turn_id":"01a086d9-1656-7222-abc3-99dd7f5f30b7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"In this branch, inspect which evidence and other log files where pushed into the repo that shouldn't be part of an open-source repo. Make a plan to clean this up and only retain evidence in a format that (e.g. JSON) that actually make sense for you to analyze and compare against later.\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08817-c8c8-7d53-8255-f9463d8a4632","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1788989655.240365,"turn_id":"01a08817-c598-7bc1-a17f-fdfc5c6ee1af"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"You will use the evidence how?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a089e7-5d43-7d30-a5f9-9d552776336d","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789020036.419014,"turn_id":"01a089e7-5a6f-77b3-95fa-079e4aa483f7"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Got it. Do you have the full plan for the cleanup?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08a0d-0845-71b3-a4e4-57abe4a799c8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789022505.029303,"turn_id":"01a08a0d-0556-7b30-b5d9-06601eedb52e"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Is your plan touching any files that did not originate from the work in this branch?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08a1a-1351-7cb0-b526-b30947d2a004","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789023359.825372,"turn_id":"01a08a1a-10ac-7752-ac63-1253a948ac15"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"\"It excludes unchanged files inherited from the baseline.\nSo it is not strictly limited to files created by this work.\" – So which one is it?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08a1a-ef69-7872-b098-356bfc4332e8","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789023416.169106,"turn_id":"01a08a1a-ec36-7702-8b89-9deaaa2aef2a"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Which files were already present?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08a1b-3d44-7291-9e4d-c2b15635d873","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789023436.100704,"turn_id":"01a08a1b-3b6a-7ee0-ad18-641a33fa8572"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Huh, I am asking with files you want to clean up that were already present before the branch existed?\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08a76-96b0-79a3-9ea8-17055d58fb2a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789029422.768075,"turn_id":"01a08a76-91aa-7a30-9c0b-c8518bf8e397"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Ok, show the plan again\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08a77-aef5-77b0-a4ec-800bc524f9c3","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789029494.517649,"turn_id":"01a08a77-ab78-75c1-ba4e-7d8af557339f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"content":[{"text":"Implement the plan, then propose a follow-up to clean history as well, in this branch only.\n","type":"input_text"}],"id":"msg_01a08a78-a844-71a0-b332-87b791c20516","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"content_item_kinds":["user.text"],"create_time":1789029558.340729,"turn_id":"01a08a78-a5d4-73b1-848e-df5dcfdaae5f"},"role":"user","type":"message"},{"call_id":"call_Cmk1q9aL6h1B97M9sUVfiJ1X","id":"fco_01a08ae7-67cd-7e80-b836-452b6a5f56fe","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"create_time":1789036816.333667,"turn_id":"01a08a78-a5d4-73b1-848e-df5dcfdaae5f"},"output":"{\"message\":\"Wait timed out.\",\"timed_out\":true}","type":"function_call_output"},{"encrypted_content":"REDACTED","id":"rs_0e42ced9de323089016aa28915db9087d289a647d34385a48a","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a08a78-a5d4-73b1-848e-df5dcfdaae5f"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"},{"content